  "question": {
    "text": "An electromagnetic wave in vacuum has the electric and magnetic fields $\\vec{E}$ and $\\vec{B}$, which are always perpendicular to each other. The direction of polarization is given by $\\vec{X}$ and that of wave propagation by $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{k}}$. Then :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "c6UgH",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{X} \\| \\vec{B}$ and $\\vec{k} \\| \\vec{B} \\times \\vec{E}$ \n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HjTH0",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{X} \\| \\vec{E}$ and $\\vec{k} \\| \\vec{E} \\times \\vec{B}$ \n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "xJBwG",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{X} \\| \\vec{B}$ and $\\vec{k} \\| \\vec{E} \\times \\vec{B}$ \n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Iq408",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{X} \\| \\vec{E}$ and $\\vec{k} \\| \\vec{B} \\times \\vec{E}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Direction of polarization is parallel to magnetic field,\n$\\therefore \\quad \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{X}} \\| \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}$\nand direction of wave propagation is parallel to $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}$\n$\\therefore \\quad \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{K}} \\| \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}$",
    "image": null
  },
